      "side": 1,
      "message": "What does setting `ProtectionId.WIDEVINE` enforce?",
      "revId": "5489e4042a48b9dee25a76018231fcf4f27dbb12",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "de57713e_0b1b7f50",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IOpaqueKey.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 58
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T21:21:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In general ProtectionIds are platform specific. For the WIDEVINE one it should enforce the same protections currently used by Widevine output video buffers (only accessible by the trusted components that will decrypt into this buffer and the one that will display it).",
      "parentUuid": "f8e1312e_4ffbd3ad",
      "revId": "5489e4042a48b9dee25a76018231fcf4f27dbb12",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "908f1af3_aa306090",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IOpaqueKey.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 58
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 2016000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-15T20:07:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Making sure I understand correctly, setting this on a key would ensure that content decrypted using the key is only output to certain buffers (with platform-dependent enforcement)? Is `set_protection_id` allowed to be called more than once for the lifetime of a key?",
      "parentUuid": "de57713e_0b1b7f50",
      "revId": "5489e4042a48b9dee25a76018231fcf4f27dbb12",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3c60ae0_5dcc48fa",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IOpaqueKey.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 58
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 2016000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-01T17:12:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it feasible to add the option to compute an opaque shared secret (that cannot be re-derived in the clear)? I saw that `hwkey_derive_versioned` does something similar with the option to derive either clear or opaque keys.",
      "revId": "5489e4042a48b9dee25a76018231fcf4f27dbb12",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9783a73e_487f6f22",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IOpaqueKey.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 58
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 1942645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-14T21:21:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It could be, depending on the requirements. If it is opaque; how are you planning to use this shared secret? Do you want to use the shared secret directly to create a key?",
      "parentUuid": "e3c60ae0_5dcc48fa",
      "revId": "5489e4042a48b9dee25a76018231fcf4f27dbb12",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7797105a_7615c1b3",
        "filename": "security/see/hwcrypto/aidl/android/hardware/security/see/hwcrypto/IOpaqueKey.aidl",
        "patchSetId": 58
      },
      "lineNbr": 92,
      "author": {
        "id": 2016000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-12-15T20:07:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For the opaque key use case, I would like to directly create an HMAC key with ECDH + HKDF. Ideally, if the underlying hardware supports it, this new key would be output directly to the hardware key table. If `calculate_shared_secret` returns the raw ECDH result, I suppose there would need to be a policy that determines if it can be invoked to prevent the opaque key from being re-derived in the clear.",
      "parentUuid": "9783a73e_487f6f22",
      "revId": "5489e4042a48b9dee25a76018231fcf4f27dbb12",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
